WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.359 --> 00:00:12.299
I first heard of Ebola on the 24th of May,
and that was the first time I went on Google

00:00:12.299 --> 00:00:20.499
and Googled what Ebola is. It was a kind of
very scary and unimaginable name. What the

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:25.189
hell is Ebola? You're trying to figure out
where did that come from? This is the very

00:00:25.189 --> 00:00:32.090
first time that Ebola has struck Sierra Leone.
So people have little or no preparedness.

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:38.480
When we first had Ebola, the area that is
affected is the opposition political party's

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:45.480
stronghold. So there were a lot of misconceptions
that 'Oh, census is coming in December. The

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:50.700
country is supposed to have census in December.
And so what these guys are trying to do right

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:57.660
now is to kill some of us and reduce the numbers.'
But then, as we get along the reality begins

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:03.870
to show itself. So denial was not an issue
anymore. It's about the level of understanding

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:10.740
and the level of literacy that people do have.
The outbreak has tremendously affected the

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:16.180
lifestyle of people. Right now, around 8 o'
clock, 9 o'clock, everyone will be running

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:22.250
home. There are no more nightclubs. There
are no more pubs. There are no more restaurants.

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:27.560
People don't shake hands anymore. People don't
hug anymore. Everyone is suspicious about

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:33.729
someone. My kids have been home
since July, and they cannot go to school because

00:01:33.729 --> 00:01:38.530
schools are not functioning. That will hamper
on the socio-economic development of the country

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:45.150
-- a country that is recovering from 11 years
brutal civil war. It's not just the Ebola

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:49.170
that is killing people in the country. It's
the poverty. It's the feeling of being left

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:57.350
alone. It's the feeling of hopelessness. Our
health system was just not prepared for an

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:04.640
emergency like Ebola. We were struggling already
on a regular basis, or on a day-to-day basis

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:12.550
in providing healthcare for people, the basic
primary health care. We have very limited

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:18.959
number of medical practitioners, especially
doctors. All the holding centers we have are

00:02:18.959 --> 00:02:25.370
full. All the hospitals are full. People die
of hypertension, people die of stress, people

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:31.330
die of common illnesses, maternity-related issues.
If you were pregnant in Sierra Leone today,

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:36.879
it would be a very difficult situation because
where do you go to hospital? People's life

00:02:36.879 --> 00:02:43.540
at risk. Nothing is working in the country.
It's as if you live in a world that everything

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:48.800
is not working, nothing is happening, and
all you're looking for is a divine grace.

